    "result_text": "The full suite passes \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class (the other files under `acceptance/` are support classes), and `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a `capacityWarning` flag that is `true` when the owner's city already holds 40\u201349 owners at create time (approaching the hard limit of 50, which is unchanged).\n\nThe change is spread across small, cohesive units, keeping structural impact low:\n\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 one added line, alongside the existing `owner.set\u2026Warning(...)` calls, reusing the existing `CityCodes.countInCity` helper: `owner.setCapacityWarning(CityCodes.countInCity(owners, owner) >= 40);`. Since the `>= 50` guard above already rejects anything at/over the limit, `>= 40` here means exactly the 40\u201349 band. No new branch, so the method's cyclomatic complexity is unchanged.\n- **`Owner`** \u2014 a new `capacity_warning` column field plus a null-safe getter/setter mirroring the existing `bulkSignupWarning` pattern (each a trivial CC-1 accessor). MapStruct maps it to the DTO automatically by name.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 a read-only `capacityWarning` boolean property so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it in the JSON response.\n- **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** / **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 added the `capacity_warning BOOLEAN` column and the matching seed value in the positional inserts.\n\nNo existing method grew in complexity; behaviour was added as small new units.",
